    {
      "policy_id": "DEMO-AML-001",
      "chunk_id": "DEMO-AML-001#001",
      "text": "Unusual transaction amount and new beneficiary review\nThis synthetic demo policy requires investigators to consider a payment unusual when its amount is materially higher than the account's established transaction pattern. A payment to a new payee is an additional risk indicator, especially for a young account. Investigators should request contextual information where the purpose, beneficiary relationship, or source of funds is not supported. A rule signal begins an investigation; it does not by itself authorize blocking, rejecting, or reporting a transaction.",
